{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/940897-iron-will","id":940897,"title":"Iron Will","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-31T16:07:21-07:00","id":940897,"title":"Iron Will","content":"<span style=\"color:#681D00\"><span style=\"font-family:P22Hopper-Edward\">Iron Will (\u2022\u2022)<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>Prerequisite: </b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Resolve \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>Effect: </b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Your character\u2019s resolve is unwavering. When spending<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Willpower to contest or resist in a Social interaction, you may<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">substitute your character\u2019s Resolve for the usual Willpower<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">bonus. If the roll is contested, roll with 8-again<br /> <br /> Does this apply to dominate/majest? I would assume so as the only other social interaction you would need to resist is the doors but as that is an optional rule to have in place if you didn't this merit would do nothing so my initial thought is this works when resisting dominate/majesty but I may be wrong, anyone know if it does or doesn't work or can enlighten me as to what it does apply to? Cheers</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12176-theboydante","name":"TheBoyDante","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T16:36:41-07:00","id":940921,"title":"","content":"There are other social interactions than Doors.<br /> <br /> Iron Will is for mundane social interactions.<br /> <br /> Indomitable is for supernatural influences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T16:58:21-07:00","id":940935,"title":"","content":"Social Maneuvering isn't really very optional. I mean, it is in the same sense that any rule in an RPG is optional, because you can run your game the way you like. But it ties into other subsystems, like some werewolf Gifts, so it's harder to remove than most subsystems in the game. That said, even if you play without Social Maneuvering, that doesn't mean there are no dice rolls for social interactions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T17:19:42-07:00","id":940949,"title":"","content":"Yea it explicitly states social maneuvering shouldn't be used on PC's as there is no option to say no, there are optional rules for this which make it easier to use on PC's and explains it in better details but is still an optional rule like combat hacks in the old armory book all being optional and not part of the system or subsystem. We are going to use them in our game but I am fairly sure it is a purely optional ruling.<br /> <br /> I imaged it would be used on more mundane things, but just seemed a bit of a useless 3 point merit with a 4 dot prerequisite as in social maneuvering you can just say no I'm not doing what you've opened all my doors I'll take a pretty harmless condition instead and gain some xp, if it worked on disciplines as they could be seen as social interactions as majesty you have to speak to an auidence, whisper words etc and dominate you have to speak to them and say what you want them to do I would have thought it was worth it's points (just) but unless explicitly stated elsewhere that it does work on disciplines I don't think I'll invest the points.<br /> <br /> Thanks for feedback!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12176-theboydante","name":"TheBoyDante","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}